> This file is a project handoff/change log. Treat source code, CI status, and GitHub history as authoritative if any status below becomes stale.

## 2026-10-13 — Experimental CPU + Vulkan inference

- Read the full `sync-ai-full-logs-gemma.txt` export before changing inference. The latest Gemma 3 4B Q4_K_M request took 262.2 seconds: 123.5 seconds prompt evaluation, 137.8 seconds generation, 26 tokens at 0.19 tokens/sec. The device snapshot showed about 823 MB system RAM available before generation.
- Add an opt-in inference acceleration preference with CPU-only (default), CPU + Vulkan with 2 GPU layers, or CPU + Vulkan with 4 GPU layers. The native loader checks for a registered Vulkan device and otherwise remains CPU-only.
- If a Vulkan-assisted model load fails, retry once with CPU-only so the existing path remains usable. Model diagnostics report requested/active GPU layer counts, detected Vulkan devices, and fallback status.
- Make the default context memory-aware: devices reporting under 5 GiB physical RAM use a 2,048-token cap; larger devices retain the 4,096-token cap. This is intended to reduce KV-cache pressure, not a guarantee of faster inference.
- Enable the llama.cpp Vulkan backend in CMake and install the shader compiler / SPIR-V headers in CI. Build compatibility and actual GPU speed remain unverified until GitHub Actions and Galaxy A16 device tests complete.
- No merge or release is performed by this work. CPU-only remains the default; GPU offload is opt-in and experimental.

## 2026-10-13 — Workspace continuation and artifact editing

- Add an in-place **EDIT SOURCE** flow for every Workspace artifact. Users can edit the artifact text and save it back to the same Workspace item; obvious incompleteness remains flagged instead of being marked complete.
- Add **CONTINUE WITH SYNC** for failed/incomplete Workspace artifacts. The continuation prompt includes the current partial source, asks the local model for only the missing fragment, appends it to the existing artifact rather than creating a duplicate, and reruns basic completeness checks. If Sync fails to return a fenced continuation, the original is left unchanged. The user can repeat continuation if the file still appears incomplete.
- Reload Workspace storage before applying edits/continuations so a stale activity instance does not overwrite a newer artifact revision.
- Existing generated artifacts, File Library flows, Memory import, chat history, and other features remain intact. Physical-device testing is still required.

## 2026-10-13 — File Library, referenced-file context, and 1024-token artifacts

- Fix the drawer's Files route: it now opens a dedicated File Library instead of sending the selected file through the memory-import request handler. The separate Personalization → Import Memory File flow remains intact.
- Add persistent app-private File Library storage with multi-select document import, SHA-256 duplicate detection, metadata, preview for readable text, export, delete, and a “Ask Sync” shortcut. Imported copies do not depend on the original SAF URI staying available. Individual files are limited to 32 MiB.
- When a message mentions a library filename (or unambiguously follows up on a recently mentioned file), attach the contents of up to two matching files to local-model context. Supported text/code formats include TXT, Markdown, CSV/TSV, JSON, XML, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Java/Kotlin, Python, YAML, SQL, logs, and similar source/text files. PDF, office, image, and other binary formats can be stored/exported but are not yet content-extracted for the local model.
- For small text-library files (up to 3,000 bytes), an unambiguous single-file edit request routes to Workspace and preserves the original filename. The original is never overwritten automatically: Workspace offers explicit replace or save-as-copy choices in File Library. Multi-file mentions can be used for analysis; full-file rewrites are handled one source file at a time.
- Raise artifact generation from 768 to 1,024 tokens, matching the existing native generation ceiling. Ordinary chat remains at 512 tokens. Validate latency and memory on the 4 GB Galaxy A16 before assuming 1,024-token artifact requests are safe for every prompt.
- Build/phone regression verification pending for this change. No release tag or release assets are changed.

## 2026-10-12 — Update consent, check intervals, voice tuning, artifact guards

- Manual update checks now always show release details and a DOWNLOAD / LATER choice; they no longer start downloads without confirmation. Automatic downloading remains configurable and defaults to off for new installs. Existing saved preferences are preserved.
- Add a persistent update-check interval selector: every 3, 6, 9, or 12 hours, every day, or every week. Checks are evaluated when Sync AI opens/resumes; this is not a background polling service.
- Add adjustable TTS pitch alongside existing speech-rate and installed Android TTS voice selection. This tunes an installed voice; it does not clone or synthesize a new voice.
- Strengthen Workspace HTML checks so static Rock-Paper-Scissors mockups without real controls, event handlers, live UI updates, and appropriate player labels are rejected as incomplete. For an explicit two-player Rock-Paper-Scissors request whose local-model draft fails those checks, use a bundled, self-contained playable HTML fallback and tell the user transparently. This remains a targeted fallback and heuristic, not a full browser execution test.
- Third-party dictation integration is not included here; a provider such as Wispr Flow needs a supported SDK or system-level speech-recognition integration and should be evaluated separately before adding dependencies.

## 2026-10-12 — Artifact quality, generation limits, and safe-area follow-up

- The exported v0.4.0 logs show long responses repeatedly reaching the exact 256-token cap. Raise normal generation to 512 tokens and artifact generation to 768 tokens, with a native hard ceiling of 1024.
- Increase native context from 2048 to 4096 tokens while keeping the CPU micro-batch at 256. Validate memory, latency, and stability on the Galaxy A16 before considering a larger context.
- Route explicit artifact requests and clear artifact follow-ups into Workspace: show progress in chat rather than duplicating source, derive a filename from the user's request, and keep the complete source in the artifact store.
- Strengthen artifact instructions to require real runnable behavior, implemented handlers, visible state/results, no placeholders/unused variables, and a self-check. Use lower sampling temperature for artifacts.
- If an artifact request ends without a complete fenced block or fails basic structural/behavior checks (including the known static Rock-Paper-Scissors failure pattern), mark the Workspace draft failed/incomplete rather than reporting it as successfully created. This is a lightweight guard, not a full runtime test of arbitrary code.
- Keep the selected Workspace source view updating in place while generation streams; do not repeatedly reload a running HTML preview. Refresh the preview when generation completes.
- Apply Android system-bar/display-cutout insets to Workspace and the Appearance studio so headers/content stay inside the safe area on edge-to-edge Android versions.
- PR #16 was merged into `fix/generation-timer-alarm-export` on 2026-10-12. The current base branch includes the generation/Workspace changes, but physical-device regression tests for the 4096-token context and artifact generation are still pending. No release tag or release assets were changed.

## 2026-10-11 — Sync Canvas / Workspace repair (in progress)

### Clarification from Sam
- Workspace is intended to be **Sync's Canvas/artifact viewer**, similar to ChatGPT Canvas or Claude Artifacts.
- It is a place for Sync to produce and show its generated work in progress or completed, not a user drawing/editor surface and not an Android file picker.
- The recent “Call Mama” / contact-call command behavior was mentioned only as an example of a previously broken feature that was fixed. **It was not the suspected cause of Workspace breaking.** Do not modify calling behavior as part of this fix.

### Root cause found on the stable v0.3.0 baseline
- The Workspace sidebar entry was wired to the Android file-picker action.
- The Canvas action itself opened Settings.
- The actual artifact-viewing Canvas behavior was missing from the stable branch.
- Therefore this was a Workspace navigation miswire plus missing functionality, not a regression caused by the call-command fix.

### Implementation committed to a separate branch
Branch: `fix/sync-workspace-canvas`

Draft PR: [#14 — Fix Sync Canvas Workspace and capture generated artifacts](https://github.com/SamYoBoi284/Sync-AI/pull/14)

Changes included in the PR:
- Route the Workspace sidebar entry to a dedicated Sync Canvas artifact viewer.
- Add persistent local storage for generated artifacts.
- Capture fenced code and document deliverables from local model responses.
- Stream draft artifacts into Workspace during generation and mark them completed or incomplete afterward.
- Provide an artifact read/preview surface.
- Preview locally generated HTML inside Sync, with a separate source view.
- Add artifact actions: copy, save to a user-chosen location, and remove from Workspace.
- Keep the existing file/memory picker and SAF import/export flows separate and intact.
- Adjust generation instructions so Sync is prompted to produce recognizable, complete artifact blocks for code, webpages, scripts, and documents.

### Safety / scope
- Work is based on `fix/generation-timer-alarm-export`, the working v0.3.0 baseline.
- Do not change the baseline branch while fixing Canvas.
- Do not remove or replace existing SAF, file import/export, model import, voice, wake-word, call, alarm, or updater functionality.
- Follow the project rule: **NEVER DELETE SOMETHING THAT ALREADY WORKS unless it directly contradicts a new requirement or is specifically being fixed.**
- PR #14 was subsequently merged into `fix/generation-timer-alarm-export` on 2026-10-12. No new version tag/release was created by that merge.
- The latest known CI attempt was GitHub Actions run **#672**, building a debug APK. At the time of this handoff, its final result and on-device verification were not confirmed. Check the live run before relying on this status.

### Outstanding physical-device verification
PR #14 and the generation/Workspace follow-up in PR #16 have merged into the development baseline, but the remaining tests below still need real-device confirmation on Sam's Galaxy A16:
1. Workspace opens Canvas, not Android's file picker or Settings.
2. Generated code/document artifacts appear in Workspace, stream safely, and finish as completed or incomplete.
3. Reopening Workspace retains artifacts; HTML preview/source view and copy/save/remove actions work.
4. Existing SAF import/export, model import, voice/wake-word, calling, alarms, and other core behavior remain intact.
5. Validate 4096-token context memory/latency and artifact generation; verify the new two-player RPS fallback when the local model returns a static mockup.
6. After PR #17 CI succeeds, test manual update consent, interval persistence, auto-download preference, and voice pitch on-device.
7. Do not publish a tag/release until the user explicitly approves and the regression tests are satisfactory.

